  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> be the sample space of all five digit numbers. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is the probability that a randomly selected number from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>, is a multiple of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> but not divisible by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0146</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2085</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0285</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1521</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given, five-digit number,</p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mi>S</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo></math>total&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;digit number will be<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></math></p><p>Now let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;number&nbsp;is multiple of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;but not divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Smallest&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;digit divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10003</mn></math></p><p>Largest&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;digit divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99995</mn></math></p><p>Now by using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;term of A.P formula we have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>99995</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10003</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>7</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12857</mn></math></p><p>Now finding number which is divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn></math></p><p>Again using A.P formula we have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>99995</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10010</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>35</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2572</mn></math></p><p>Now number divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;but not by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn></math>&nbsp;are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12857</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2572</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10285</mn></math></p><p>So, probability will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10285</mn><mn>90000</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0285</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
